the initial character design for the  first sonic the hedgehog film was met  with overwhelming backlash in 2019 and  it seems like the video game turned film  was doomed however after being delayed  by paramount so the team could redesign  the titular blue hedgehog the film went  on to have a record setting opening  weekend now with two sequels and a  spin-off series on the horizon the  adaptation has successfully turned  things around the reception for the new  final trailer for sonic the hedgehog 2  is a whole lot warmer than the original  much maligned trailer with many fans  eager to see what's next for the  franchise jim carrey who seldom stars  and sequels will even be returning as  the evil mad scientist dr evo eggman  robotnik the upcoming adventure film  will follow sonic voiced by ben schwartz  as he faces off against avenge for  robotnik  this time though each has a partner in  crime tales voiced by colleen  o'shaughnessy and knuckles voiced by  idris elba if sonic and tails don't beat  robotnik and knuckles to the master  emerald it could mean the end of the  world with the stakes higher than ever  the final trailer for sonic the hedgehog  2 offers another glimpse of the  explosive search for this all-powerful  emerald here's what you might have  missed in the action-packed new trailer  sonic the hedgehog has always had a  rocking soundtrack in the newest trailer  for sonic 2 one of the first scenes  shows james marston's thomas wachowski  attending a wedding in hawaii but right  in the middle of the ceremony his phone  rings  so help me thomas sorry sorry  astute fans may have picked up on this  auditory cue but for the uninitiated the  ringtone is actually the music from the  first level of the original sonic video  game this little tune comes to us from  the green hill zone which was also  referenced in the first film as the town  sonic hides in green hills montana one  of the major driving forces of both the  sonic movies and video games are  mysterious stones known as chaos  emeralds in the trailer we see that dr  robotnik has discovered what he refers  to as a source of ultimate power which  is revealed to be the green chaos  emerald these particular gems within the  game series are imbued with fantastic  powers like time manipulation or the  ability to transform its holder into a  being of vast cosmic power as  illustrated by sonic's yellow third  iteration that is effectively  unstoppable in the video game sonic 3.  sonic wishes to protect the chaos  emeralds while dr robotnik wants to use  that power to remake the world in his  twisted image knuckles is the official  guardian of these powerful relics and  his tribe of anthropomorphic animals is  tasked with protecting them the trailer  sees dr robotnik use a chaos emerald to  power his army of machines while also  radiating the awesome power of the  emeralds himself which is illustrated by  the green arcs of lightning across his  body hopefully this means that we might  get a glimpse of super sonic at some  point in sonic 2. as long time sonic  gamers have been pointing out online  there's a moment in the new trailer that  is almost identical to a classic sonic  the hedgehog 2 level called the sky  chase zone in which tales and sonic  operate a red and white biplane dubbed  the tornado through various obstacles  and enemies in the new trailer we see  nearly a shot for shot recreation of it  with sonic even standing on top of the  plane's wings just like he does in the  game while sonic the hedgehog found a  place in the gaming world as sega's  answer to nintendo's mario it resembled  most early 90s games by focusing more on  the gameplay than the storyline  collecting golden rings and avoiding  obstacles all while going really fast  wasn't something that essentially needed  a story in those days however in a small  throwback moment from the new trailer  audiences were treated to a sweet call  back to the game that changed all of  that in a moment with epic slow motion  and an obligatory shout out to the mcu  oh great the winner soldier  sonic jumps from a cave at the top of a  mountain and uses a makeshift snowboard  to flee from pursuers when sonic jumps  on his board he lets out to recognizable  cheer  the exclamation goes back to 1998 with  the release of sonic adventure which was  the first to truly introduce 3d gameplay  the first to be story driven and the  first include a full voiceover including  sonic's little cheer  [Music]  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite stuff are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

